Patch crosvm: scanout modifier.

The guest scans out with SET_SCANOUT_BLOB, which carries format/strides/offsets but no modifier, and crosvm
imported such buffers into the display as modifier 0 (linear). Buffers from the minigbm gralloc are usually UBWC
(DRM_FORMAT_MOD_QCOM_COMPRESSED), so the panel showed tile garbage. Take the modifier rutabaga recorded at
allocation (resource3d_info) when there is one.

diff --git a/devices/src/virtio/gpu/virtio_gpu.rs b/devices/src/virtio/gpu/virtio_gpu.rs
index 7592c9b10..0d6a72daf 100644
--- a/devices/src/virtio/gpu/virtio_gpu.rs
+++ b/devices/src/virtio/gpu/virtio_gpu.rs
@@ -482,7 +482,11 @@ impl VirtioGpuScanout {
                 data.drm_format,
                 data.strides[0],
                 data.offsets[0],
-                0,
+                // mothershipOS: SET_SCANOUT_BLOB has no modifier; use the one from allocation (UBWC)
+                rutabaga
+                    .resource3d_info(resource.resource_id)
+                    .map(|q| q.modifier)
+                    .unwrap_or(0),
             ),
             None => {
                 let query = rutabaga.resource3d_info(resource.resource_id).ok()?;
